  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Define \\(x \\diamond y\\) to be \\(|x - y|\\) for all real numbers \\(x\\) and \\(y.\\) What is the value of\n\n\\[(1 \\diamond (2 \\diamond 3)) - ((1 \\diamond 2) \\diamond 3)?\\]",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(-2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(-1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(0\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(2\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "a",
    "value": "-2"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12b-2022-p1.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Since \\(2 \\diamond 3 = |2-3| = 1,\\) we get \\(1 \\diamond (2 \\diamond 3) = 1 \\diamond 1 = 0.\\)\n\nSince \\(1 \\diamond 2 = |1-2| = 1,\\) we get \\((1 \\diamond 2) \\diamond 3 = 1 \\diamond 3 = |1-3| = 2.\\)\n\nThe value is \\(0 - 2 = -2.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Evaluate the inner \\(\\diamond\\) first, using \\(a \\diamond b = |a-b|\\)",
        "Compute \\(1 \\diamond (2 \\diamond 3)\\) and \\((1 \\diamond 2) \\diamond 3\\) separately, then subtract"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
